{"input":"Graph contract: kind=graph. nodes contains distinct strings. edges contains [from,to,cost] triples with positive integer fuel costs and at most one edge per ordered pair. start and goal are nodes; fuel is a nonnegative integer. plan is an ordered list of destination node names. Every edge is directed. Start at {node:start,fuel:fuel}. An action is legal exactly when an edge from the current node to its destination exists and its cost is at most the remaining fuel. A legal move changes node to its destination and subtracts the edge cost. At the first illegal action, include that action's {legal:false,after:unchanged_state} step, stop immediately, and do not evaluate subsequent actions. An empty plan is valid. valid means every proposed action was legal. reaches_goal is true exactly when the whole plan is valid and its terminal node is goal, including an initially satisfied goal with an empty plan. shortest_plan is a fresh plan from the INITIAL state that reaches goal within initial fuel, minimizes the number of moves, and breaks ties by the lexicographic order of the entire destination-name sequence. It is [] for an initially satisfied goal and null if no feasible plan exists. Fuel cost is a feasibility constraint, not the optimization objective. Return exactly a JSON object with steps:[{legal:boolean,after:{node:string,fuel:integer}}], after:{node:string,fuel:integer}, valid:boolean, reaches_goal:boolean, shortest_plan:list_or_null. Include only evaluated steps.\nTask JSON:\n{\"kind\":\"graph\",\"nodes\":[\"Beryl\",\"Dune\",\"Ember\",\"Aster\",\"Cedar\"],\"edges\":[[\"Beryl\",\"Dune\",1],[\"Dune\",\"Ember\",4],[\"Ember\",\"Aster\",1],[\"Aster\",\"Cedar\",3],[\"Dune\",\"Beryl\",1],[\"Beryl\",\"Aster\",1],[\"Beryl\",\"Cedar\",4],[\"Cedar\",\"Ember\",2]],\"start\":\"Beryl\",\"goal\":\"Cedar\",\"fuel\":9,\"plan\":[\"Dune\",\"Beryl\",\"Dune\",\"Beryl\",\"Dune\",\"Beryl\",\"Dune\",\"Beryl\",\"Dune\",\"Beryl\",\"Dune\",\"Beryl\",\"Dune\",\"Beryl\",\"Dune\",\"Beryl\",\"Dune\",\"Beryl\",\"Dune\",\"Beryl\",\"Cedar\"]}","target":{"after":{"fuel":0,"node":"Dune"},"reaches_goal":false,"shortest_plan":["Cedar"],"steps":[{"after":{"fuel":8,"node":"Dune"},"legal":true},{"after":{"fuel":7,"node":"Beryl"},"legal":true},{"after":{"fuel":6,"node":"Dune"},"legal":true},{"after":{"fuel":5,"node":"Beryl"},"legal":true},{"after":{"fuel":4,"node":"Dune"},"legal":true},{"after":{"fuel":3,"node":"Beryl"},"legal":true},{"after":{"fuel":2,"node":"Dune"},"legal":true},{"after":{"fuel":1,"node":"Beryl"},"legal":true},{"after":{"fuel":0,"node":"Dune"},"legal":true},{"after":{"fuel":0,"node":"Dune"},"legal":false}],"valid":false}}
{"input":"Graph contract: kind=graph. nodes contains distinct strings. edges contains [from,to,cost] triples with positive integer fuel costs and at most one edge per ordered pair. start and goal are nodes; fuel is a nonnegative integer. plan is an ordered list of destination node names. Every edge is directed. Start at {node:start,fuel:fuel}. An action is legal exactly when an edge from the current node to its destination exists and its cost is at most the remaining fuel. A legal move changes node to its destination and subtracts the edge cost. At the first illegal action, include that action's {legal:false,after:unchanged_state} step, stop immediately, and do not evaluate subsequent actions. An empty plan is valid. valid means every proposed action was legal. reaches_goal is true exactly when the whole plan is valid and its terminal node is goal, including an initially satisfied goal with an empty plan. shortest_plan is a fresh plan from the INITIAL state that reaches goal within initial fuel, minimizes the number of moves, and breaks ties by the lexicographic order of the entire destination-name sequence. It is [] for an initially satisfied goal and null if no feasible plan exists. Fuel cost is a feasibility constraint, not the optimization objective. Return exactly a JSON object with steps:[{legal:boolean,after:{node:string,fuel:integer}}], after:{node:string,fuel:integer}, valid:boolean, reaches_goal:boolean, shortest_plan:list_or_null. Include only evaluated steps.\nTask JSON:\n{\"plan\":[\"Dune\",\"Beryl\",\"Dune\",\"Beryl\",\"Dune\",\"Beryl\",\"Dune\",\"Beryl\",\"Dune\",\"Beryl\",\"Dune\",\"Beryl\",\"Dune\",\"Beryl\",\"Dune\",\"Beryl\",\"Dune\",\"Beryl\",\"Dune\",\"Beryl\",\"Cedar\"],\"fuel\":9,\"goal\":\"Cedar\",\"start\":\"Beryl\",\"edges\":[[\"Beryl\",\"Dune\",1],[\"Dune\",\"Ember\",4],[\"Ember\",\"Aster\",1],[\"Aster\",\"Cedar\",3],[\"Dune\",\"Beryl\",1],[\"Beryl\",\"Aster\",1],[\"Beryl\",\"Cedar\",4],[\"Cedar\",\"Ember\",2]],\"nodes\":[\"Beryl\",\"Dune\",\"Ember\",\"Aster\",\"Cedar\"],\"kind\":\"graph\"}","target":{"after":{"fuel":0,"node":"Dune"},"reaches_goal":false,"shortest_plan":["Cedar"],"steps":[{"after":{"fuel":8,"node":"Dune"},"legal":true},{"after":{"fuel":7,"node":"Beryl"},"legal":true},{"after":{"fuel":6,"node":"Dune"},"legal":true},{"after":{"fuel":5,"node":"Beryl"},"legal":true},{"after":{"fuel":4,"node":"Dune"},"legal":true},{"after":{"fuel":3,"node":"Beryl"},"legal":true},{"after":{"fuel":2,"node":"Dune"},"legal":true},{"after":{"fuel":1,"node":"Beryl"},"legal":true},{"after":{"fuel":0,"node":"Dune"},"legal":true},{"after":{"fuel":0,"node":"Dune"},"legal":false}],"valid":false}}
